## Key Decisions
- Upstox V3 LTP uses `instrument_key` parameter with `NSE_EQ|ISIN` (pipe + ISIN) format — `NSE_EQ:SYMBOL` (colon) format failed; API response keys are `NSE_EQ:SYMBOL`
- Upstox Analytics Token has no API call limits, making it ideal as primary price source; multiple instruments can be batched in one request via comma-separated `instrument_key` values
- ISIN stored on `Symbol` entity (populated from NSE CSV column 6 during symbol refresh) — `UpstoxPriceFetcher` resolves from `SymbolRepository` first, `HoldingRepository` fallback; works even if no user holds the stock yet
- `stock_price_history` table stores OHLC for EQUITY/ETF and NAV (close only) for MUTUAL_FUND with source=`AMFI`; GOLD/SGB uses gold price API
- AMFI historical NAV endpoint (`portal.amfiindia.com/DownloadNAVHistoryReport_Po.aspx?tp=1`) used — 1-day chunk size due to large per-response size (~40K lines/day for all schemes)
- `collectMfIsins()` prioritizes holding ISINs first then symbol table ISINs — reduces backfill scope to actually-needed data
- Async backfill (`triggerBackfill` with `@Async`) returns immediately; frontend polls `GET /backfill-mf-status` every 3s and auto-refreshes chart on completion
- `ConcurrentHashMap.put()` NPE on null value — always use `.put(key, nonNullValue)` or `.clear()` before re-populating status map
- Net worth history auto-snapshots on first `investment-over-time` call if empty — no need for user to visit Net Worth page first
- Investment growth `getValueForAssetType()` maps: EQUITY/ETF → `equityValue`, GOLD/SGB → `goldValue`, everything else → `debtValue` (from net worth snapshot Redis data)
- Daily scheduled backfill at 3 AM covers last 5 days; initial large backfill requires hitting `POST /api/v1/market/backfill-mf-history` endpoint once
- Chart line color dynamic: green (`#22c55e`) when change ≥ 0, red (`#ef4444`) when change < 0
- Lightweight Charts v5 uses unified `addSeries(SeriesDefinition, options)` API instead of old shorthand methods (`addCandlestickSeries` removed)
- Rolldown bundler (Vite 8) fails on `</>` fragment syntax — use `<div>` wrapper instead
- TradingView free embed widgets do NOT support NSE data — only BSE with EOD data is available for India
- `ResponsiveContainer` with `height="100%"` returns `width(-1) height(-1)` on remount when parent hasn't laid out — fix: use explicit pixel `height={256}`
- Lightweight Charts `chart.remove()` throws `removeChild` error when container is detached from DOM — wrap cleanup in try-catch

